WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
1 · Create a Message automation. In Shortcuts, open Automation. Tap +, then choose Message.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:25.000
2 · Match your bank's wording. We use “purchase” as an example. Enter a phrase or currency code that appears in YOUR bank alerts.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:35.000
3 · Run automatically. Leave Sender as Any Sender. Choose Run Immediately, then tap Next.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:45.000
4 · Create a blank shortcut. Tap Create New Shortcut under Get Started.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:57.000
5 · Add the bank import action. Search for Import Bank Message. Tap the TrackExpenses action.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:12.000
6a · Tap the Message field. Tap the blue Message placeholder inside the import action. A variable bar opens at the bottom.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:24.000
6b · Tap Select Variable. At the bottom, tap Select Variable. If the keyboard is open, look just above it.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:41.000
6c · Choose Shortcut Input. Tap the blue Shortcut Input beneath “Receive messages as input”. This passes the incoming SMS to the action.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:52.000
6d · Check the connection. The action now says Shortcut Input. Do not type those words yourself. Tap × to close the variable bar.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:04.000
7 · Keep imports quiet. Tap the arrow beside the action. Turn Show When Run off.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:12.000
8 · Save your automation. Tap the blue checkmark. Matching bank alerts will now reach TrackExpenses.
